       "text": "---\ntitle: API Rate Limiting in ADS: Limits by User Type\nshare_url:
     https://demo.sourcegraph.com/deepsearch/e6992090-5d50-4f37-ad32-f9543abba2a2\ncreated: 2026-06-06T07:55:12Z\nupdated:
     2026-06-06T07:56:29Z\n---\n\n# How does API rate limiting work in ADS? What are the rate limits for different user types?\n\nNow I
     have a thorough picture. Here is a complete explanation:\n\n---\n\n## ADS API Rate Limiting\n\n### Architecture Overview\n\nRate
     limiting in ADS is implemented in the [api_gateway](r/github.com/adsabs/api_gateway) service, built on top of
     [flask-limiter](https://flask-limiter.readthedocs.io/). The core logic lives in
     [`apigateway/services.py`](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/adsabs/api_gateway/-/blob/apigateway/services.py) in the
     `LimiterService` class, backed by **Redis** as the storage backend (fixed-window strategy by default).\n\n---\n\n### How Limits Are
     Declared\n\nEach microservice (solr-service, biblib-service, etc.) declares its rate limits in its views via the `flask_discoverer`
     `@advertise` decorator:\n\n```python\n# github.com/adsabs/solr-service – solr/views.py\nclass Search(SolrInterface):\n    scopes =
     []\n    rate_limit = [5000, 60*60*24]   # [count, window_in_seconds]\n    decorators = [advertise('scopes',
     'rate_limit')]\n```\n\nWhen the API gateway starts up, it fetches each microservice's `/resources` document and registers every
     endpoint with a `shared_limit` decorator using the advertised `rate_limit` values ([`services.py`
     L464-469](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/adsabs/api_gateway/-/blob/apigateway/services.py?L464-L469)).\n\n---\n\n###
     Per-Endpoint Rate Limits\n\n| Endpoint | Limit per day |\n|---|---|\n| `GET /search/query` (Search) | **5,000** |\n| `POST
     /search/bigquery` (BigQuery) | **100** |\n| `GET /search/qtree` | **500** |\n| `GET /search/tvrh` | **500** |\n| Most other endpoints
     (biblib, objects, journals, graphics, etc.) | **1,000** |\n\nSources:
     [`solr/views.py`](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/adsabs/solr-service/-/blob/solr/views.py?L33-L690), [`biblib/views/library
     _view.py`](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/adsabs/biblib-service/-/blob/biblib/views/library_view.py?L28-L31).\n\n---\n\n###
     Per-User-Type Rate Limits\n\nRate limits are **multiplied per OAuth client** using a `ratelimit_multiplier` column on the
     `OAuth2Client` model ([`models.py`
     L110](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/adsabs/api_gateway/-/blob/apigateway/models.py?L110)):\n\n```python\nclass
     OAuth2Client(base_model, OAuth2ClientMixin):\n    ratelimit_multiplier = sa.Column(sa.Float, default=1.0)\n
     individual_ratelimit_multipliers = sa.Column(sa.JSON)   # per-endpoint overrides\n```\n\nOn every request, `_calculate_limit_value()`
     computes the actual limit as:\n\n```\neffective_limit = base_count * ratelimit_multiplier\n```\n\n([`services.py`
     L713-743](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/adsabs/api_gateway/-/blob/apigateway/services.py?L713-L743))\n\nThe **user types**
     and their effective multipliers:\n\n| User Type | `ratelimit_multiplier` | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Anonymous** (`anonymous@ads`)
     | **≤ 1.0** (set to `-1` in DB quota, treated as lowest tier) | Gets a temporary bootstrap token (expires in 24h). Uses remote IP as
     the rate-limit scope if no token. |\n| **Regular authenticated user** | **1.0** (default) | Scoped by `email:client_id`. Default quota
     of `2.0` total across all their OAuth clients. |\n| **Elevated / API user** | **> 1.0** (set manually by admins) | `ratelimit_quota`
     on `User` controls the maximum sum of multipliers across all their clients ([`services.py`
     L345](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/adsabs/api_gateway/-/blob/apigateway/services.py?L345-L360)). |\n| **Bot tokens** |
     Routed to separate Solr handler (`BOT_SOLR_SERVICE_*`) | Identified by their token appearing in `BOT_TOKENS` config; still subject to
     limits but through a dedicated Solr backend ([`solr/views.py`
     L664-676](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/adsabs/solr-service/-/blob/solr/views.py?L664-L676)). |\n\nIndividual endpoints
     can also have their own per-user multiplier overrides via `individual_ratelimit_multipliers` (a JSON map of endpoint regex patterns to
     multiplier values).\n\n---\n\n### Rate Limit Scope (Keying)\n\nThe scope function ([`services.py`
     L817-838](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/adsabs/api_gateway/-/blob/apigateway/services.py?L817-L838)) determines who the
     limit is counted against:\n\n- **OAuth token present**: `\"{email}:{client_id}\"` — limits are per client, not per user globally\n-
     **Authenticated session (no token)**: `\"{email}\"`\n- **Anonymous / unauthenticated**: **remote IP address**\n\n---\n\n### Scaling
     Cost (Heavy Query Penalty)\n\nWhen `LIMITER_SERVICE_SCALING_COST_ENABLED = True` ([`config.py`
     L81](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/adsabs/api_gateway/-/blob/apigateway/config.py?L81)), slow requests above the
     `SCALING_COST_THRESHOLD` (default: 100 requests) cost more than 1 unit against the rate limit. The cost is calculated as:\n\n```\ncost
     = 1 + min(floor(log2(request_time / mean_time) * 5), 9)\n```\n\nSo a request twice as slow as the mean costs 6, three times as slow
     costs ~9. This penalizes expensive queries without lowering the global limit for fast queries ([`services.py`
     L745-784](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/adsabs/api_gateway/-/blob/apigateway/services.py?L745-L784)).\n\n---\n\n###
     Response Headers\n\nEvery rate-limited response includes these headers (visible with `curl -v`):\n\n```\nX-RateLimit-Limit:
     5000\nX-RateLimit-Remaining: 4999\nX-RateLimit-Reset: <UTC timestamp>\n```\n\nLimits reset at **midnight UTC** daily. See the
     [developer API docs README](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/adsabs/adsabs-dev-api/-/blob/README.md?L57-L79) for more.\n\n##
     Sources\n\n- [ADS API rate limiting rate limit user
     types](/search?q=patterntype:nls%20ADS%20API%20rate%20limiting%20rate%20limit%20user%20types)\n- [repo:^github.com/adsabs rate limit
     user type anonymous](/search?q=patterntype:nls%20repo:%5Egithub.com%2Fadsabs%20rate%20limit%20user%20type%20anonymous)\n-
     [repo:github.com/adsabs rate_limit](/search?q=patterntype:keyword%20repo:github.com%2Fadsabs%20rate_limit)\n-
     [github.com/adsabs/api_gateway/apigateway/services.py@e91143b?L690-800](/github.com/adsabs/api_gateway@e91143b1fd24472ead03cf8f7960edf
     a7f7e9d1f/-/blob/apigateway/services.py?L690-800)\n- [github.com/adsabs/api_gateway/apigateway/config.py@e91143b](/github.com/adsabs/a
     pi_gateway@e91143b1fd24472ead03cf8f7960edfa7f7e9d1f/-/blob/apigateway/config.py)\n- [github.com/adsabs/api_gateway/apigateway/models.p
     y@e91143b](/github.com/adsabs/api_gateway@e91143b1fd24472ead03cf8f7960edfa7f7e9d1f/-/blob/apigateway/models.py)\n-
     [github.com/adsabs/api_gateway/apigateway/views.py@e91143b?L490-680](/github.com/adsabs/api_gateway@e91143b1fd24472ead03cf8f7960edfa7f
     7e9d1f/-/blob/apigateway/views.py?L490-680)\n- [github.com/adsabs/api_gateway/apigateway/services.py@e91143b?L300-440](/github.com/ads
     abs/api_gateway@e91143b1fd24472ead03cf8f7960edfa7f7e9d1f/-/blob/apigateway/services.py?L300-440)\n- [github.com/adsabs/solr-service/so
     lr/views.py@dc7c877?L1-80](/github.com/adsabs/solr-service@dc7c8772274f9b6d3d82a1510cc07769e529a9dd/-/blob/solr/views.py?L1-80)\n-
     [github.com/adsabs/solr-service/solr/views.py@dc7c877?L640-720](/github.com/adsabs/solr-service@dc7c8772274f9b6d3d82a1510cc07769e529a9
     dd/-/blob/solr/views.py?L640-720)\n- [github.com/adsabs/api_gateway/apigateway/services.py@e91143b?L440-560](/github.com/adsabs/api_ga
     teway@e91143b1fd24472ead03cf8f7960edfa7f7e9d1f/-/blob/apigateway/services.py?L440-560)\n-
     [github.com/adsabs/api_gateway/apigateway/services.py@e91143b?L560-695](/github.com/adsabs/api_gateway@e91143b1fd24472ead03cf8f7960edf
     a7f7e9d1f/-/blob/apigateway/services.py?L560-695)\n- [repo:github.com/adsabs/api_gateway _key_func _scope_func ratelimit_multiplier](/
     search?q=patterntype:keyword%20repo:github.com%2Fadsabs%2Fapi_gateway%20_key_func%20_scope_func%20ratelimit_multiplier)\n-
     [repo:github.com/adsabs/adsabs-dev-api rate
     limit](/search?q=patterntype:keyword%20repo:github.com%2Fadsabs%2Fadsabs-dev-api%20rate%20limit)\n-
     [github.com/adsabs/api_gateway/apigateway/services.py@e91143b?L800-860](/github.com/adsabs/api_gateway@e91143b1fd24472ead03cf8f7960edf
     a7f7e9d1f/-/blob/apigateway/services.py?L800-860)\n- [github.com/adsabs/adsabs-dev-api/README.md@2e221c0?L55-85](/github.com/adsabs/ad
     sabs-dev-api@2e221c0fea2a5668b4c4769d3413079e7859f883/-/blob/README.md?L55-85)\n\n"
     }

