       10 # ADS Core Systems Overview
       11
       12 ## Authentication (OAuth 2.0)
       13
       14 **Primary mechanism**: Flask-oauthlib based OAuth 2.0 provider in `adsws/modules/oauth2server/`
       15
       16 ### Token Types:
       17 - **Anonymous/bootstrap tokens**: 24h expiry, auto-created for unauthenticated frontend users
       18 - **User tokens (BB client)**: Long-lived (expires ~year 2500), one per authenticated user
       19 - **Personal API tokens**: Long-lived, manageable via `/accounts/token`, for direct API usage
       20 - **Opaque tokens**: Generated via `gen_salt(40)`, stored in database (NOT JWTs)
       21
       22 ### Authentication Flow:
       23 1. **Bootstrap endpoint** (`/oauth/authorize`): Entry point for Bumblebee frontend
       24    - Unauthenticated → auto-login as special `BOOTSTRAP_USER_EMAIL`, mint temp token
       25    - Authenticated → create/return long-lived client+token
       26    - Uses Flask `SecureCookieSession` (signed with `SECRET_KEY`) to store `oauth_client` ID
       27
       28 2. **Username/password login**: `POST /accounts/user/login` → validates credentials, calls `flask-login`
       29 3. **Email confirmation**: HMAC-signed tokens via `itsdangerous.TimedSerializer`
       30 4. **Registration**: Requires reCAPTCHA + email confirmation
       31
       32 ### Frontend (Nectar/Next.js):
       33 - Uses `iron-session` (encrypted HTTP-only cookies) on top of OAuth tokens
       34 - Stores: `token` (OAuth + user data), `isAuthenticated`, `apiCookieHash` (PBKDF2)
       35
       36 **Key files**:
       37 - `adsws/modules/oauth2server/provider.py` — OAuth provider
       38 - `adsws/accounts/views.py` — Bootstrap, login, registration
       39 - `nectar/src/pages/api/auth/login.ts` — Frontend auth integration
       40
       41 ---
       42
       43 ## Rate Limiting (per user type)
       44
       45 **Architecture**: `api_gateway` service using `flask-limiter` with Redis backend (fixed-window)
       46
       47 ### Per-Endpoint Daily Limits:
       48 - Search API: 5,000 requests
       49 - BigQuery: 100 requests
       50 - Most others: 1,000 requests
       51
       52 ### User Type Multipliers:
       53 | User Type | Multiplier | Details |
       54 |---|---|---|
       55 | Anonymous | ≤ 1.0 | Gets bootstrap token (24h), scoped by IP if no token |
       56 | Authenticated (default) | 1.0 | Scoped by `email:client_id`, max quota 2.0 total |
       57 | Elevated/API users | > 1.0 | Set manually by admins via `ratelimit_quota` |
       58 | Bot tokens | separate Solr handler | Identified by `BOT_TOKENS` config |
       59
       60 ### Scaling Cost (optional):
       61 - When enabled, slow queries above threshold cost more (logarithmic penalty)
       62 - Query 2x slower = costs 6 units; 3x slower = ~9 units
       63
       64 ### Response Headers:
       65 ```
       66 X-RateLimit-Limit: 5000
       67 X-RateLimit-Remaining: 4999
       68 X-RateLimit-Reset: <UTC timestamp>
       69 ```
       70 Limits reset at **midnight UTC** daily.
       71
       72 **Key files**: `api_gateway/services.py` (LimiterService), `api_gateway/models.py` (OAuth2Client.ratelimit_multiplier)
       73
       74 ---
       75
       76 ## Saved Searches (myADS) — vault service
       77
       78 **Repo**: `github.com/adsabs/vault`
       79
       80 ### Data Storage:
       81 PostgreSQL tables:
       82 - `users` → user ID, preferences (JSONB `user_data`), optional link server
       83 - `queries` → serialized Solr queries keyed by MD5 hash (`qid` = md5(user_id + query))
       84 - `myads` → notification setups (templates or raw queries)
       85
       86 ### Notification Types:
       87 - `type='query'`: raw saved Solr query
       88 - `type='template'`: structured alerts (arxiv, citations, authors, keyword)
       89 - `frequency`: daily or weekly
       90 - `stateful`: tracks new results since last check
       91 - `active`: enable/disable toggle
       92
       93 ### Query Construction:
       94 - Raw queries: stored as binary blobs
       95 - Template queries: built dynamically at execution time with date ranges
       96   - **arxiv**: filters by `bibstem:arxiv`, `arxiv_class`, `entdate`
       97   - **citations**: wraps in `citations(...)`
       98   - **authors**: applies date windows to author query
       99   - **keyword**: generates 3 queries (recent, trending, most cited)
      100
      101 ### Key Endpoints:
      102 - `POST/GET /query/<qid>` — store/retrieve queries
      103 - `GET/PUT/DELETE /notifications/<id>` — manage notification setups
      104 - `GET /notification_query/<id>` — execute query for a setup
      105 - `GET /get-myads/<user_id>` — fetch full profile for pipeline
      106
      107 ---
      108
      109 ## User Libraries (Paper Collections) — biblib-service
      110
      111 **Repo**: `github.com/adsabs/biblib-service`
      112
      113 ### Data Storage:
      114 PostgreSQL tables:
      115 - `user` → ADS absolute UIDs → local IDs
      116 - `library` → UUID ID, name, description, public/private, bibcodes (JSON dict)
      117 - `permissions` → join table (read, write, admin, owner flags)
      118 - `notes` → per-bibcode notes, versioned via `sqlalchemy-continuum`
      119
      120 ### Design:
      121 - Library IDs are **UUIDs**
      122 - Bibcodes stored as **JSON dict** with timestamp of addition
      123 - Both library and notes are **version-tracked** (change history)
      124
      125 ### API Structure (biblib/views/):
      126 - `library_view.py` → get/add/remove bibcodes
      127 - `document_view.py` → per-document ops
      128 - `permission_view.py` → manage collaborator access
      129 - `operations_view.py` → set operations (union, intersection, difference)
      130 - `notes_view.py` → CRUD per-bibcode notes
      131 - `classic_view.py` → import from ADS Classic
      132 - `transfer_view.py` → ownership transfer
      133 - `user_view.py` → list user's libraries
      134
      135 ### Key Distinction:
      136 - `vault.library_id` ≠ `biblib.library` — vault's is OpenURL link server registry
      137 - Actual paper collections live entirely in `biblib-service`
      138
      139 ---
      140
      141 ## Microservice Ecosystem
      142
      143 Key repos:
      144 - **adsws**: OAuth provider, bootstrap, user accounts, web services
      145 - **api_gateway**: Proxies & rate-limits all API calls to microservices
      146 - **vault**: myADS saved searches, notifications, user preferences
      147 - **biblib-service**: User libraries/collections
      148 - **solr-service**: Search backend
      149 - **other services**: objects, journals, graphics, ADSAff, ADSOrcid, etc.
      150
      151 Frontend: **nectar** (Next.js) or **Bumblebee** (legacy Angular)
      152
      157 - `adsabs/adsws` — Core web services + OAuth provider
      158 - `adsabs/vault` — Saved searches & notifications
      159 - `adsabs/biblib-service` — User libraries
      160 - `adsabs/api_gateway` — Rate limiting & API proxying

